settings-indexers-title = Indexers for exact usages (level 2)
settings-indexers-note = Which tools CodeSkimr finds on this computer. CodeSkimr installs nothing itself; if something is missing, the command to copy is shown with it.
settings-indexers-check-again = Check again
settings-indexers-checking = Checking …
settings-indexers-checked = Last checked: { $when }
settings-indexer-memory-title = Memory per indexer
settings-indexer-memory-note = The most memory in MB that one indexer may use. 0 means it follows the general limit. A new value counts from the next scan; a scan that is running keeps its value. A Node.js indexer (scip-typescript) gets three quarters of the value as its heap, so 8,192 MB means a heap of 6,144 MB. A large TypeScript project can need far more than the other indexers.
settings-indexer-memory-field = Memory limit of { $name } in MB
settings-indexer-memory-follows = follows the general limit of { $limit } MB
settings-indexer-memory-save = Save
settings-indexer-memory-reset = Use the default
settings-indexer-memory-saved = Saved. It counts from the next scan.
settings-indexer-memory-failed = Could not be saved.
settings-indexer-memory-invalid = Enter a whole number from 0 to { $max }.
settings-indexer-memory-by-flag = A command line flag sets this value; a saved value has no effect while it is used.
settings-indexers-failed = The indexers could not be checked. Is CodeSkimr still running?
